{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-25T05:51:21.704Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1778"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1778: pm context extension_health reports ok for packages with a known update and prints same-named project and global copies as identical rows"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1778 (filed 2026-11-24). pm context ends with an extension_health block whose rows are {name,status}: status comes only from static discovery, so a package with a known newer registry version reads ok, and a package installed in both project and global scope prints two identical rows with nothing saying which copy the runtime loads (project shadows global by name in buildEffectiveExtensions). pm context is the orientation call agents run first, so ok: 3 reads as nothing to do; the report's hub ran extensions seven weeks behind for that reason. Constraint: pm context must stay offline and fast, and update lookups are network calls that pm package manage and pm package doctor make but never persist (last_update_remote_version is documented as never persisted). Companion finding in the same command: an invalid --section value is refused with a recovery bundle that lists only 8 of the 10 valid sections and says allowed_values_omitted: 2 (complete domain via SDK error.context.recovery.allowed_values), which a CLI agent cannot read; the human Next steps line lists all 10. Small closed domains should print whole. Reproduced on 2026.11.25. Duplicate check: searched extension_health update available shadowed scope, recovery allowed values omitted; no open owner."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","context","extensions","gh:1778","packages","recovery"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-25T05:51:21.704Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-25T05:51:21.704Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"extension_health rows carry name, scope, version and status, plus the last observed newer registry version as update when one is known, without any network call from pm context; The summary carries updates_available and a next hint naming the update command only when that count is above zero; A copy shadowed by a same-named copy in another scope is marked shadowed_by instead of repeating an identical row; A refused enumerated value whose whole domain is small prints every allowed value in the recovery bundle, with no omitted counter"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"unbraind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"pm context tells an agent which installed packages have known updates and which copy is active, offline, and a refused section lists every valid section"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"5ce5ecfab2e1c2131ffff80005a2af3e0e01365e2d40b874a84b22cf986a7eb2","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status"