{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-25T08:10:28.117Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_delete","patch":[{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/comments/2"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-25T08:10:28.117Z"}],"before_hash":"170f829a4534019a69ac9b061372d3c8728b76eb077466e89cbd0955ac313ef6","after_hash":"bedda4e92c9436869c1060f3db67f40af1efb8861f18a46a93cdf8719c18c862","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ebe4397ecd5708cbae19201fa1bc7a349d7e7ac795b13482c25ce508076b99c2"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-25T08:47:44.219Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-25T08:47:44.219Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 2 (Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh: 1 P1, 10 P2, 5 P3), each verified and fixed. Hints: one targeted command per loaded package (at most five) rendered as pm [--pm-path <absolute tracker>] package upgrade --<scope> --packages-only -- <name>: the name after -- cannot be re-read by the bootstrap key=value normalizer (P1, probed: status=open stays a literal target), --packages-only keeps a lost target from upgrading the CLI, no scope-wide upgrade of unreported packages, the absolute tracker survives SDK cwd swaps, and --no-extensions is never inherited (it would fail activation verification). Writer: under the lock the record is rebuilt from the managed state on disk, keeping the latest observation per current installation and dropping replaced or removed ones, which closes the stale-process overwrite race, bounds the file, and is refused above 1 MiB. Reader: O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK open with fstat and a bounded read on the descriptor (no FIFO hang, no swapped-file widening); runtime/ rechecked after the lock is held; checked_at must parse. Downgrade guard uses SemVer precedence against the installed npm version (prereleases sort first). Context treats corrupt managed metadata as unknown updates instead of failing. Inventory binds identity to the directory's own managed record."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-25T08:47:44.219Z"}],"before_hash":"bedda4e92c9436869c1060f3db67f40af1efb8861f18a46a93cdf8719c18c862","after_hash":"3e5acbde28e9533716563bf26150fede996c2611c8668f350d85ba8abcbf9a46","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a3ab4c01a28c39eb527eb64c3c018dd471a703eadf4056eeeaa95b57acd9b913"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-25T09:57:02.442Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-25T09:57:02.441Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 3 (Codex: 1 P1, 9 P2, 2 P3). Design change that closes a whole class: next no longer names packages. Each hint is the live, scoped check pm [--pm-path <absolute tracker>] package manage --<scope>, whose remediation names the upgrade, so no manifest-controlled name can select a second installation (manifest name equal to another package's npm name), parse as an option (-- --global, -- --version), or lose its quoting; Markdown renders hints as code spans so CommonMark never consumes shell escapes. Also fixed: local npm artifacts (path or file: specs, shared isLocalNpmSpec rule with upgrade) never get a registry update; the reader lstat-checks the entry before the no-follow open, which covers Windows where O_NOFOLLOW is undefined; the observation lock passes maxWaitMs so PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS cannot stretch the derived write; inventory binds observations to the exact directory. Not changed, with reason: replacing runtime/ with a link between the post-lock recheck and the rename needs write access to the tracker's own runtime directory, which already controls tracker state; Node has no openat for directory-relative I/O, and the recheck plus link refusal bound the window."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-25T09:57:02.442Z"}],"before_hash":"3e5acbde28e9533716563bf26150fede996c2611c8668f350d85ba8abcbf9a46","after_hash":"926907962bf5755cc890f4a1449f62c5c0d1e54b567e41461dc1393efcd34e2e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"72deedceef134e4ee1442cd4f00535ba313b182b376e100df1acceea38be1896"}
